# Normalise line endings.
#
# This repository was authored on Windows and every tracked text file was
# stored with CRLF. Nothing enforced that, so any tool writing LF — an editor
# with a different default, a script, a CI job — rewrote whole files and turned
# one-line changes into thousand-line diffs.
#
# LF is the storage format from here on: it is the norm for JS/TS projects, it
# is what the Linux hosts building and serving this site use, and it means a
# diff shows what actually changed.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text; `eol=lf` fixes the ending for
# everything it decides is. Binary files are listed explicitly below rather
# than left to detection, because a mistake there corrupts the file.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Images. Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.JPG binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary

# Fonts and other binaries, for when they arrive.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
